# Compiled programs: lumen writes the binary into the working directory,
# named for its source and with no extension to tell it apart.
# Named one by one because a compiled program has no extension to match on,
# and every example adds another. Two of these (rag, run-agent) were committed
# before this list existed -- 8 MB each, in the history for good now, which is
# the reason the list is worth keeping current.
#
# Every one of them is anchored with a leading slash, because a bare name here
# matches at any depth, not just beside this file. `evals` used to be bare, and
# it swallowed routes/ops/evals/ along with the binary: three source files were
# written there and never added, api.ts imported a controller that was not in
# the repository, and the test job has been red ever since. The binaries all
# sit in this directory, so the slash says so.
/api
/mount-mcp
/call-model
/run-agent
/rag
/run-with-tools
/delegate
/delegate-traced
/prompt-ab
/evals
/stored-credential
/zz*
/.lumen-*
/api.backup-*

# The other binaries this package compiles, and the copies kept beside them
# while a deployment is being replaced. `api` was already named; these were
# not, which is how a 57 MB `api.prev` came to be sitting in `git status`
# looking like source. A binary that reaches a commit is in the history for
# good -- the note at the top of this file is about exactly that.
/scheduler
/indexer
# One poller per bot, built the same way and just as unwelcome in a diff.
/trigger-poller
/api.prev*
/api.pre-*
# Python bytecode, wherever the tools directory grows one.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/probe*
# The copies kept beside `indexer` while a deployment is replaced, and the
# build-time duplicate of api.ts. Same reasoning as api.prev* above: a binary
# that reaches a commit is in the history for good, and api-build.ts is a copy
# of a file that is already tracked.
/indexer.prev*
/indexer.running-*
/api-build.ts
